# Override Omarchy's default power-profile udev rule with a debounced version.
#
# The ROG Flow Z13 emits spurious power_supply events. AC0.online in particular
# flaps 0 <-> 1 every 1-3 seconds while the battery is actively charging (proven
# by the wifi-powersave rule toggling 101 times in 14 minutes while capacity
# rose monotonically 53% -> 64%). Each event triggers a profile set -> asusd
# fan curve rewrite -> momentary fan stop, plus notification spam.
#
# This rule triggers on the system battery rather than Mains. BAT0.status
# reflects actual power flow and stays stable while AC0 flaps, so the flap
# never reaches the debounce script at all.
#
# KERNEL=="BAT*" matches the kernel's system-battery names (BAT0, BAT1, ...) and
# excludes peripheral batteries such as the Elan touchpad's
# hid-0018:04F3:43C7.0008-battery-7. It is used instead of ATTR{scope}!="Device"
# because BAT0 has no scope attribute at all, and udev match semantics for a
# missing attribute are not worth relying on.
#
# The script itself re-checks type=Battery and skips scope=Device devices, so
# this rule only needs to be broad enough to catch real status changes.
#
# NOTE: No fixed --unit name — each udev event gets a unique auto-generated unit.
# A fixed name (e.g. --unit=omarchy-power-profile) causes collisions at boot
# when multiple supplies fire simultaneously, making every invocation after the
# first fail with "unit already exists".
SUBSYSTEM=="power_supply", KERNEL=="BAT*", ATTR{type}=="Battery", RUN+="/usr/bin/systemd-run --no-block --collect --property=After=power-profiles-daemon.service __HOME__/.local/share/omarchy/bin/omarchy-powerprofiles-set-debounced"
